  <main>
    <section class="intro section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">HOME SERVER / A BUILD LOG</p>
      <h1>A server built instead of rented.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A cloud server? My budget prescribed a screwdriver. So I built a small private platform at home and learned every layer the hard way.</p>
    <button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section>

    <section class="section-shell split-section">
      <div class="homelab-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">THE PREMISE</p>
        <h2>Cloud hosting promised convenience. My wallet filed an objection.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="homelab-copy">
          <p>I started with a simple plan: assemble the machine, install Linux, and learn each layer by making it work. The plan grew into working configuration, scripts, dashboards, documentation, and a repeatable operating routine.</p>
          <p>What began as “install Linux and run a few experiments” became a tiny datacenter with a power button. The useful part was not avoiding every failure. It was learning how to make failures visible, recoverable, and safe to explain publicly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="chapters" class="section-shell story-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE BUILD, IN CHAPTERS</p>
        <h2>Pick a tile. Follow the rabbit hole.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Each chapter pairs the engineering decision with the problem that made it necessary. Nothing here includes private addresses, credentials, keys, tokens, or unique device identifiers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-grid">
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="origin"><span class="tile-number">01</span><span class="tile-icon">✦</span><strong>Why build it?</strong><small>Cloud hosting promised convenience. My wallet filed an objection.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="hardware"><span class="tile-number">02</span><span class="tile-icon">▦</span><strong>Choosing the parts</strong><small>Enough power for experiments, not a datacenter fantasy.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="boot"><span class="tile-number">03</span><span class="tile-icon">◉</span><strong>Making it boot</strong><small>Firmware, Secure Boot, and the first negotiation.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="linux"><span class="tile-number">04</span><span class="tile-icon">⌘</span><strong>Installing Linux</strong><small>Headless Ubuntu and a CLI-first operating habit.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="access"><span class="tile-number">05</span><span class="tile-icon">↗</span><strong>Keeping access private</strong><small>SSH keys, firewall boundaries, and Tailscale.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="debugging"><span class="tile-number">06</span><span class="tile-icon">⌁</span><strong>Debugging the invisible</strong><small>Bluetooth, routes, permissions, and misleading symptoms.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="power"><span class="tile-number">07</span><span class="tile-icon">⚡</span><strong>Surviving power loss</strong><small>NUT, a UPS, graceful shutdown, and a real unplug test.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="observability"><span class="tile-number">08</span><span class="tile-icon">◒</span><strong>Seeing the system</strong><small>Docker, Prometheus, Grafana, and alerts.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="storage"><span class="tile-number">09</span><span class="tile-icon">▤</span><strong>Trusting the storage</strong><small>Health checks, LVM, encrypted backups, and restore tests.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="flashpoint"><span class="tile-number">10</span><span class="tile-icon">◇</span><strong>Putting it to work</strong><small>Flashpoint: a small service with metrics and load tests.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="public"><span class="tile-number">11</span><span class="tile-icon">◎</span><strong>Making it public safely</strong><small>A portfolio story without publishing the house keys.</small></button>
        <button class="story-tile" data-story="lessons"><span class="tile-number">12</span><span class="tile-icon">↺</span><strong>What I learned</strong><small>Verify state, change one thing, keep going.</small></button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell">
      <div class="feature-card next-card"><div class="card-kicker">NEXT CHAPTER</div><h3>More services, same rules.</h3><p>The platform is ready for self-hosted applications and local AI experiments. New services will be added one at a time, monitored from the start, and kept behind the same private access boundary.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>Docker Compose</span><span>Prometheus</span><span>Grafana</span><span>Private by default</span></div><a class="text-link" href="services/">Explore Services &amp; Experiments →</a></div>
    </section>
